    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/223725": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Financial Aid Counselor McMinnville Campus - McMinnville, OR 97128 Apply Overview Salary Range $43,000.00 - $44,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full-Time Job Shift Day Education Level None Travel Percentage None Category Finance and Administration Apply Description Financial Aid Counselor Linfield University | Financial Aid Office Reports to: Director of Financial Aid Location: McMinnville, Oregon Position Summary Linfield University is seeking a detail-oriented, student-focused Financial Aid Counselor to join our Financial Aid Office. This position plays an important role in helping students and families navigate the financial aid process by providing knowledgeable guidance, exceptional customer service, and support in understanding available financial aid opportunities. The Financial Aid Counselor is responsible for evaluating financial aid applications, determining student eligibility, administering federal, state, and institutional aid programs, and ensuring compliance with applicable regulations. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong analytical and problem-solving skills, sound judgment, and a commitment to supporting students from diverse backgrounds in achieving their educational goals. Key Responsibilities Financial Aid Advising and Student Support Advise prospective, incoming, and current students and their families on financial aid programs, scholarships, eligibility requirements, and application procedures. Provide clear, accurate information and assist students and families in resolving financial aid concerns with professionalism, empathy, and sound judgment. Represent the Financial Aid Office at campus events, including orientations, admitted student programs, and FAFSA/ORSAA completion workshops. Communicate with students regarding missing documentation, eligibility requirements, award adjustments, and other financial aid matters. Ensure students receive required exit counseling information upon graduation, withdrawal, or enrollment below half-time. Financial Aid Processing and Compliance Review and evaluate FAFSA applications and supporting financial documentation to determine student eligibility for federal, state, and institutional financial aid. Complete verification reviews, including analysis of income, household information, and other required documentation, while ensuring accuracy and regulatory compliance. Apply professional judgment when appropriate, maintaining thorough documentation and justification for decisions. Monitor and conduct initial reviews of Return to Title IV (R2T4), Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP), and course withdrawal notifications. Maintain accurate student records and protect confidential information in accordance with FERPA and applicable regulations. Exercise independent judgment and attention to detail to ensure accurate awarding, prevent funding errors, and maintain institutional compliance. Financial Aid Program Administration Reconcile Federal Work-Study, Federal Pell Grant, and Oregon state financial aid programs, including the Oregon Opportunity Grant. Administer and award OSAC scholarships, Ford Family scholarships, and other applicable last-dollar scholarship programs. Coordinate the awarding of endowed and donated scholarships, partnering with University Advancement on donor notifications and the establishment of new scholarship funds. Monitor TEACH Grant eligibility, including academic requirements, documentation, and exit counseling notifications. Administer federal and private education loan processes, including Parent PLUS, Graduate PLUS, and private loan certifications, and resolve discrepancies between university and federal systems. Collaboration and Professional Development Collaborate with campus partners, including Admissions, Academic Affairs, Athletics, the Business Office, the Registrar's Office, and University Advancement, to support student success and efficient financial aid operations. Stay current on federal and state financial aid regulations, policies, and best practices through ongoing professional development and participation in relevant training opportunities. Contribute to a collaborative, service-oriented team environment and assist with additional responsibilities as assigned. Qualifications Required Qualifications Experience working with financial documents, data management, or administrative processes requiring a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail. Strong computer skills, including proficiency with Microsoft Office applications such as Word, Excel, and PowerPoint, and the ability to learn specialized financial aid systems. Ability to interpret and apply complex policies, procedures, and regulations. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain complex information clearly and effectively. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to exercise sound judgment and manage competing priorities. Demonstrated ability to provide excellent customer service, resolve concerns professionally, and work effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Commitment to maintaining confidentiality and handling sensitive student and financial information appropriately. Willingness and ability to work occasional evenings and weekends to support university events and activities. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. Experience working in higher education, financial aid administration, or a related student services environment. Knowledge of federal and state financial aid programs, eligibility requirements, and compliance regulations. Experience with financial aid management systems and federal platforms, including Ellucian Colleague, NSLDS, COD, and CPS or their successor systems. Bilingual and bicultural skills that support effective communication with students and families from diverse backgrounds. Why Join Linfield University? At Linfield University, you'll be part of a welcoming, collaborative community dedicated to student success and lifelong learning. Our Financial Aid Office plays a vital role in making higher education accessible and helping students pursue their academic and personal goals. As a Financial Aid Counselor, you'll have the opportunity to make a meaningful difference by guiding students and families through important financial decisions while contributing to Linfield's mission of connecting learning, life, and community. About Linfield University Founded in 1858, Linfield University is an independent, comprehensive institution of higher education with campuses in McMinnville and Portland, Oregon, as well as online programs. Known for its commitment to academic excellence, personalized education, and experiential learning, Linfield prepares students to lead lives of purpose and impact. Linfield University values diversity and strives to create an inclusive environment that honors different perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences. We welcome applicants who share our commitment to fostering a respectful, supportive, and engaged campus community. PLEASE NOTE: We are hiring for  EITHER a Senior Financial Aid Counselor OR a Financial Aid Counselor.  If you meet the qualifications for both positions, please APPLY TO BOTH POSITIONS Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/223710": {
      "title": "Senior Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Senior Financial Aid Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Senior Financial Aid Counselor McMinnville Campus - McMinnville, OR 97128 Apply Overview Salary Range $45,000.00 - $47,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full-Time Apply Description Senior Financial Aid Counselor Linfield University | Financial Aid Office Position: Senior Financial Aid Counselor Department: Financial Aid Office Reports To: Director of Financial Aid Join the Linfield University Team! Linfield University is seeking a knowledgeable, detail-oriented, and student-focused Senior Financial Aid Counselor to join our Financial Aid Office. This position plays an important role in helping students and families navigate the financial aid process, understand their funding options, and access the resources needed to achieve their educational goals. The ideal candidate is a collaborative professional who enjoys working with students and families, has strong analytical and problem-solving skills, and is committed to providing exceptional customer service while ensuring compliance with federal, state, and institutional financial aid regulations. Position Summary The Senior Financial Aid Counselor provides comprehensive financial aid advising and support to prospective, incoming, and current students and their families. This position is responsible for evaluating financial aid applications, determining student eligibility, administering federal and state financial aid programs, and ensuring the accurate and timely awarding of financial assistance. Working closely with colleagues across the university, the Senior Financial Aid Counselor exercises independent judgment in interpreting complex financial aid regulations, resolving student concerns, and supporting the effective administration of financial aid programs. This role requires exceptional attention to detail, strong communication skills, and a commitment to student success. Key Responsibilities Financial Aid Advising and Student Support Provide personalized financial aid guidance to prospective, new, and continuing students and their families throughout the application and awarding process. Explain financial aid eligibility requirements, scholarships, grants, loans, and other funding opportunities in a clear and accessible manner. Review financial aid applications and supporting documentation to verify financial and household information reported on the FAFSA. Apply federal financial aid regulations, relevant IRS tax requirements, and institutional policies to determine student eligibility. Exercise professional judgment when evaluating unique student circumstances, documenting decisions and justifications as appropriate. Respond to student and family concerns with professionalism, empathy, and effective conflict-resolution skills. Represent the Financial Aid Office at university events, including orientation programs, admitted student events, and FAFSA/ORSAA completion workshops. Financial Aid Administration and Compliance Complete initial financial aid verification reviews, identify missing documentation, and communicate requirements to students. Ensure accurate and timely processing of financial aid awards in compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations. Reconcile federal work-study funds and oversee the reconciliation and appropriate awarding of Federal Pell Grants and Oregon state financial aid programs, including the Oregon Opportunity Grant. Monitor and conduct initial reviews of Return to Title IV (R2T4), Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP), and course withdrawal or drop notifications. Ensure students receive required exit counseling information upon graduation, withdrawal, or enrollment below half-time. Monitor TEACH Grant eligibility, including academic progress, GPA requirements, required documentation, and exit counseling notifications. Maintain accurate student records and safeguard confidential information in accordance with FERPA and applicable regulations. Exercise sound judgment and meticulous attention to detail to minimize errors, maintain compliance, and protect student and institutional eligibility. Scholarship and Loan Management Administer and award scholarships through the Oregon Student Aid Commission (OSAC) and last-dollar scholarship programs, including Ford Family scholarships. Determine recipients of endowed and donor-funded scholarships based on established eligibility criteria. Collaborate with University Advancement to coordinate donor notifications and assist with establishing new scholarship funds. Oversee the administration and certification of federal and private education loans for CPS, including Parent PLUS, Graduate PLUS, and private student loans. Identify and resolve loan processing discrepancies between university systems and the U.S. Department of Education. Collaboration and Professional Development Build positive working relationships with university partners, including Admission, Academic Support, faculty, Athletics, the Business Office, the Registrar's Office, and University Advancement. Participate in state, regional, and national professional development opportunities to remain current on financial aid regulations, policies, and best practices. Stay informed about changes to federal and state financial aid programs and apply updated requirements to daily operations. Contribute to a collaborative, service-oriented office environment focused on accuracy, efficiency, and student success. Perform other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Qualifications Minimum of one year of experience in a higher education setting, preferably in financial aid, admission, or enrollment services. Familiarity with financial documents and strong computer and technology skills. Ability to interpret and apply complex financial aid regulations, policies, and procedures. Strong analytical skills, exceptional attention to detail, and the ability to maintain accuracy while managing competing priorities and interruptions. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated problem-solving abilities and sound judgment in decision-making. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Commitment to providing outstanding customer service to students and families from diverse backgrounds. Comfort with public speaking and presenting financial aid information to groups. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive student information appropriately. Availability to work occasional evenings and weekends to support university events and student needs. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree. Bilingual and bicultural skills. Experience working directly with financial aid programs and eligibility determination. Proficiency with financial aid and student information systems, including Ellucian Colleague, NSLDS, COD, CPS, and Microsoft Office applications such as Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Why Join Linfield University? At Linfield University, you'll be part of a welcoming, collaborative, and mission-driven community dedicated to helping students thrive. Our Financial Aid Office plays a vital role in making a Linfield education accessible and supporting students throughout their academic journeys. As a Senior Financial Aid Counselor, you'll have the opportunity to make a meaningful difference by helping students and families understand their financial aid options, overcome financial barriers, and pursue their educational goals. Linfield values diverse perspectives, encourages professional growth, and fosters a supportive environment where employees can contribute their skills and expertise to student success. Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion Linfield University is committed to fostering an inclusive community that values diverse backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We strive to create an environment that honors academic freedom, celebrates diverse cultures, encourages mutual respect, and affirms the value of every individual. We welcome applicants who share our commitment to creating an equitable and supportive educational environment for all students. Apply Today! If you're passionate about helping students achieve their educational goals, enjoy navigating complex financial aid processes, and thrive in a collaborative, student-centered environment, we encourage you to apply for the Senior Financial Aid Counselor position at Linfield University. Join us in making higher education more accessible and helping students build a brighter future! PLEASE NOTE: We are hiring for  EITHER a Senior Financial Aid Counselor OR a Financial Aid Counselor.  If you meet the qualifications for both positions, please APPLY TO BOTH POSITIONS Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree preferred. Bilingual and bicultural preferred. Sr. Counselor with at least one year in a higher education setting, preferably within financial aid, admission, or enrollment. Familiar with financial documents and high competency in computer skills. Proficiency in technology and systems used to determine students' eligibility and originate financial aid awards, including but not limited to Colleague, NSLDS, COD, CPS, MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc. Ability to interpret complex financial aid regulations and apply them appropriately in different situations. Comfortable with public speaking and working with diverse families. Ability to work independently as well as in a team environment. Strong interpersonal skills. Strong problem-solving abilities and the ability to use sound judgment for decision-making. Some evening and weekend work required. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/223420": {
      "title": "Senior Manager-Career Partnerships",
      "description": "Senior Manager-Career Partnerships You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Senior Manager-Career Partnerships McMinnville Campus - McMinnville, OR 97128 Apply Overview Salary Range $60,000.00 - $60,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full-Time Job Shift Day Education Level Bachelor's Degree Travel Percentage Negligible Category University Advancement Apply Description Senior Manager of Career Partnerships Linfield University | University Advancement Position Type: Full-Time (1.0 FTE) FLSA Status: Exempt Department: University Advancement Reports To: Vice President for University Advancement Effective Date: October 2026 Position Summary Linfield University is seeking a dynamic, collaborative and relationship-driven Senior Manager of Career Partnerships to lead its Center for Career and Life Design. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced professional who is passionate about connecting students with meaningful career opportunities, building strong employer partnerships and helping students successfully transition from college to career. Reporting to the Vice President for University Advancement, the Senior Manager provides strategic leadership for the Center while taking an active, hands-on role in employer engagement, career development and student support. This position is responsible for expanding Linfield's network of local, regional and national employers, creating high-value internships and career opportunities, and strengthening connections between academic programs and professional pathways. The Senior Manager serves as the Center's primary liaison to the University's graduate and professional programs, including the School of Business, School of Nursing and Education Department. Working closely with Academic Affairs, University Advancement, alumni, parents and industry partners, this position helps ensure Linfield students are prepared to succeed in an evolving workforce. As a leader and active contributor, the Senior Manager supervises two professional staff members, oversees Center operations and advances initiatives that support student career readiness, experiential learning and strong postgraduate outcomes. The Center also provides career development resources to recent alumni. Key Responsibilities Employer and Industry Partnerships (35%) Build, cultivate and maintain strong relationships with local, regional and national employers to expand internship, externship, job shadowing and full-time employment opportunities for Linfield students. Strategically grow Linfield's employer network by leveraging connections with alumni, parents, trustees and other University partners. Develop employer-sponsored projects, recruiting partnerships and hiring pipelines that connect students with meaningful professional experiences. Plan and lead career fairs, employer panels, networking events and other opportunities that bring students and employers together. Maintain accurate employer engagement records and track recruitment and placement outcomes using CatConnect/Handshake and related systems. Collaborate with University Advancement to align employer and corporate outreach with broader constituent engagement and fundraising strategies. Partner closely with the Senior Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement to engage alumni, parents and other constituents in supporting student career success. Graduate and Professional Program Partnerships (30%) Serve as the primary career development liaison to Linfield's graduate and professional programs, building collaborative relationships with deans, program directors and faculty. Provide individualized career counseling and guidance to students pursuing specialized professional pathways. Develop and deliver classroom presentations, career workshops and professional development programming tailored to specific academic disciplines. Connect students and academic programs with relevant employers, industry professionals and alumni to strengthen internship and employment opportunities. Support the development of industry-specific recruiting relationships and career pathways that align with students' academic and professional goals. Team Leadership and Center Operations (20%) Provide leadership, supervision, coaching and performance evaluation for the Manager of Experiential Learning Opportunities and Career Advisor. Establish strategic goals, priorities and initiatives that advance the Center's mission and support University objectives. Oversee the Center's budget, technology systems, policies, programming and annual calendar. Develop and monitor measures of success, including internship participation, employer engagement, student satisfaction and postgraduate career outcomes. Collect, analyze and communicate results to inform program improvements and demonstrate the Center's impact. Ensure career development services and resources are available to recent Linfield alumni. Represent the Center for Career and Life Design in meetings with University leadership, trustees, employers and other external partners. Academic Affairs Collaboration (10%) Partner with academic deans, faculty and advisors to integrate career exploration, professional development and career readiness into the student academic experience. Collaborate with academic programs to expand experiential learning opportunities, internships and classroom-based career programming. Align career development initiatives with academic objectives and the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) career readiness competencies. Additional Responsibilities (5%) Perform other duties as assigned to support University Advancement and the broader mission of Linfield University. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in business, communications, public relations or a related field. Minimum of five years of relevant professional experience in employer relations, career services, corporate partnerships, recruiting or a related field. Demonstrated success developing, expanding and sustaining productive relationships with employers and external partners. Experience supervising employees or leading professional teams. Excellent written and verbal communication, interpersonal and presentation skills. Strong organizational skills, sound judgment and the ability to independently manage competing priorities. Ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues, faculty, University leadership and external partners in a goal-oriented team environment. Experience using data to evaluate program effectiveness, measure outcomes and communicate results. Flexibility to work occasional evenings and weekends as needed. Valid driver's license, satisfactory driving record and ability to obtain and maintain certification to operate Linfield University vehicles. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in higher education, student affairs, counseling or a related field. Professional experience working in a college or university career center. Established network of employers and industry contacts in the Pacific Northwest. Familiarity with career services technology and CRM platforms, including CatConnect/Handshake or comparable systems. Work Environment and Physical Requirements This position primarily works in an office environment, with regular interaction with students, faculty, staff, employers and external partners. The role may require travel to meetings, conferences, recruiting events and other professional activities. Essential physical requirements include prolonged sitting, frequent standing and walking, climbing stairs, and repetitive hand and wrist movements associated with computer work. Occasional lifting, carrying, pushing or pulling of materials weighing up to 40 pounds may be required, along with occasional exposure to outdoor weather conditions when traveling between campus buildings. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. Why Join Linfield University? At Linfield University, we believe education should open doors to meaningful careers, lifelong learning and opportunities to make a difference. As a member of University Advancement, the Senior Manager of Career Partnerships plays an important role in helping students turn their academic experiences into successful professional futures. This position offers the opportunity to lead a dedicated team, build lasting relationships with employers and alumni, and create career pathways that have a direct impact on student success and social mobility. You'll join a collaborative, mission-driven community that values innovation, personal connections and the transformative power of a Linfield education. Help shape the future of career development at Linfield University and make a lasting difference in the lives of our students and alumni. Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion Linfield University is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive community that values diverse backgrounds, experiences and perspectives. We believe that diversity enriches the educational experience, strengthens our community and contributes to academic and professional excellence. We encourage applications from individuals who share our commitment to creating an environment of mutual respect, belonging and opportunity for all students, faculty and staff. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
  },
